.nh
.TH "GUMROAD" "1" "Sep 2026" "Gumroad" "Gumroad CLI"

.SH NAME
gumroad-admin-purchases-cancel-subscription - Cancel the subscription on a purchase as an admin


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgumroad admin purchases cancel-subscription  [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Cancel the subscription linked to a purchase. The buyer email is required as a
sanity check against the purchase record.

.PP
Defaults to buyer-initiated cancellation, matching the admin web UI. Pass
--by-seller to record the cancellation as seller-initiated. The cancellation is
always attributed to the admin actor regardless of the by-seller flag.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--by-seller\fP[=false]
	Record cancellation as seller-initiated (default is buyer-initiated)

.PP
\fB--email\fP=""
	Buyer email (required)

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for cancel-subscription


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--debug\fP[=false]
	Enable debug logging to stderr

.PP
\fB--dry-run\fP[=false]
	Preview mutating requests without executing them

.PP
\fB--jq\fP=""
	Filter JSON output with a jq expression

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	Output as JSON

.PP
\fB--no-color\fP[=false]
	Disable color output

.PP
\fB--no-image\fP[=false]
	Disable image rendering

.PP
\fB--no-input\fP[=false]
	Disable interactive prompts

.PP
\fB--non-interactive\fP[=false]
	Run in explicit CI/agent mode

.PP
\fB--page-delay\fP=0s
	Wait between paginated --all requests (e.g. 200ms, 1s)

.PP
\fB--plain\fP[=false]
	Output as plain tab-separated text

.PP
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP[=false]
	Suppress non-essential output

.PP
\fB--yes\fP[=false]
	Skip confirmation prompts


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  gumroad admin purchases cancel-subscription 12345 --email buyer@example.com
  gumroad admin purchases cancel-subscription 12345 --email buyer@example.com --by-seller
  gumroad admin purchases cancel-subscription 12345 --email buyer@example.com --yes
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBgumroad-admin-purchases(1)\fP
